{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-80","kind":"proposition","title":"构造与求解：可公度量与截差无理线段与中项无理线段","englishTitle":"To a first apotome of a medial straight line only one medial straight line can be annexed which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a rational rectangle.","book":10,"number":80,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.80","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.80/","group":"prop_2","sourceNumber":80,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","contentId":"euclid-10-80","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b9a9b9bde33afe7add5794a306092d387be4a47b6bb3a0ce34f05f485d4192ce","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-80.statement","euclid-10-80.construction.1","euclid-10-80.proof.1","euclid-10-80.proof.2","euclid-10-80.proof.3","euclid-10-80.proof.4","euclid-10-80.conclusion","euclid-10-80.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-80.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6e593045f87db182e26b358863706935350581c27e848a2b14fc3b179cbbcd56","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"To a first apotome of a medial straight line only one medial straight line can be annexed which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a rational rectangle."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"中项无理线段只可把可公度只作为附件,正方形只作为整体,有理 矩形只作为整体；这里涉及截差无理线段。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-80.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c66c47ea2fd32d51a6f4ff4f3e8b9b9ba965d92bdbf0c3653253722d98cd1fbf","citations":["euclid-10-74"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let AB be a first apotome of a medial straight line, and let BC be an annex to AB; therefore AC, CB are medial straight lines commensurable in square only and such that the rectangle AC, CB which they contain is rational; [[X. 74](/principles/euclid-10-74)] I say that no other medial straight line can be annexed to AB which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a rational area."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"AB成为中项无理线段中的头截差无理线段,BC成为AB的附件;因此,AC、CB和中项无理线段属于中项无理线段,它们包含的矩形、AC、CB属于有理;我说,其他中项无理线段不得附于AB,即可公度,仅含整个正方形,并包含整个有理面积。 [[X. 74](/principles/euclid-10-74)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-80.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f6ccee194621d20903bd79ba5014c96551ad02f05d5390342b29606e4ef5fa4f","citations":["euclid-10-74"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if possible, let DB also be so annexed; therefore AD, DB are medial straight lines commensurable in square only and such that the rectangle AD, DB which they contain is rational. [[X. 74](/principles/euclid-10-74)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能的话,将DB件也列为附件;因此,AD、DB件为中项无理线段、平方可公度而长度不可公度件,其中的矩形 AD、DB件为有理件。 [[X. 74](/principles/euclid-10-74)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-80.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"14e480650c87f82a204a95a19653faa7a1f8d382eac781963bcdf2a2493eb035","citations":["euclid-2-7"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since the excess of the squares on AD, DB over twice the rectangle AD, DB is also the excess of the squares on AC, CB over twice the rectangle AC, CB, for they exceed by the same, the square on AB, [[II. 7](/principles/euclid-2-7)] therefore, alternately, the excess of the squares on AD, DB over the squares on AC, CB is also the excess of twice the rectangle AD, DB over twice the rectangle AC, CB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,由于AD比正方形的AD超出DB,DB比矩形比AD的两倍多,DB也是AC比正方形的CB,矩形比AC超出两倍,CB因为两者的比矩形比AB超出正方形,AB,因此,从另一个角度讲,AD比正方形比AC比正方形高出正方形,DB也是矩形比AD比AD高出两倍,DB比矩形比矩形比AC高出两倍。 [[II. 7](/principles/euclid-2-7)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-80.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"007a3f9713cb0725a6b4166d0240ceeffdcc85de35e637e6b618a40bd762da4f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But twice the rectangle AD, DB exceeds twice the rectangle AC, CB by a rational area, for both are rational."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是矩形 AD,DB的两倍 超过矩形 AC,CB乘以有理面积, 两者均为有理。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-80.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"80917eab3322f31bc7823d56df01800d1fd0fba405f932b5d5febb44d97b2b06","citations":["euclid-10-15","euclid-10-26"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the squares on AD, DB also exceed the squares on AC, CB by a rational area. which is impossible, for both are medial [[X. 15 and 23, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-15)], and a medial area does not exceed a medial by a rational area. [[X. 26](/principles/euclid-10-26)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,AD,DB的正方形比AC,CB乘以有理面积,这是不可能的,因为两者都为中项无理线段,中项无理线段区域不超过中项无理线段乘以有理面积。 [[X. 15 and 23, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-15)] [[X. 26](/principles/euclid-10-26)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-80.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":6,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-80.source","contentId":"euclid-10-80","revisionId":"euclid-10-80@raw-b9a9b9bde33afe7a","order":7,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f060b3c08b7b02c5bac8947ee439c5b4013ea110c8444ca6f10eed3cdeb6447e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.80/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.80\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-80:euclid-10-74:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-80","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-80.construction.1",